    acidDissociation    "chemistry/aqueousSpeciation/taurine-pKa1|pKa2.candidate.dat (recordId taurine-pKa1 [ESTIMATE, flagged], taurine-pKa2)";
    isoelectricPoint    "chemistry/aqueousSpeciation/taurine-pI.candidate.dat (recordId taurine-pI) -- itself an estimate, flagged there";
    chargeAtPH7         "DELETED as DERIVED -- never stored";
    partialMolarVolume  "aqueous V2 at infinite dilution, FLAGGED approximate (transcribe digit-exact from Millero, Lo Surdo & Shin, J. Phys. Chem. 82 (1978) 784 / Mishra & Ahluwalia, J. Phys. Chem. 88 (1984) 86) -- carried inside the derivation{} block of the diffusion record above";
    cosmoSurface        "no evidence record -- LVPP ships no COSMO output for taurine";
}

speciationNote  "strong-acid ampholyte: the sulfonate is deprotonated across the WHOLE NF/RO pH window, so Donnan exclusion is driven by a PERMANENT fixed anionic centre, unlike the alpha-carboxylate amino acids.  The van't Hoff factor is not a plain integer.  Every number behind this statement lives in the referenced dissociation records.";
